				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-f81d8b3 elementor-widget__width-initial elementor-widget-mobile__width-inherit elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="f81d8b3" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<p><span class="TextRun SCXW152036479 BCX8" lang="EN-US" xml:lang="EN-US" data-contrast="none"><span class="NormalTextRun SCXW152036479 BCX8">The huckl</span><span class="NormalTextRun SCXW152036479 BCX8">eberry is Idaho&rsquo;s official </span><span class="NormalTextRun ContextualSpellingAndGrammarErrorV2Themed SCXW152036479 BCX8">state</span><span class="NormalTextRun SCXW152036479 BCX8"> fruit</span><span class="NormalTextRun SCXW152036479 BCX8">. Huckleberries only grow wild in the cool, mountainous regions of the Pacific Northwest, making them a true treasure in Idaho.</span></span></p>								</div>
				</div>
				</div>
					</div>
				</div>
								</div>
